---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`Privacy Policy for ${site.companyName} (${site.brand}) — what information we collect through this website, how we use it, and the rights you have over your data.`}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="legal">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="updated">Last updated: 25 October 2026</p>

        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>{site.companyName}</strong> (&ldquo;{site.brand}&rdquo;,
          &ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo; or &ldquo;our&rdquo;) collects, uses, stores and protects
          personal information when you visit <strong>{site.domain}</strong> or contact us through this
          website, by email, or by messaging applications. We are a business-to-business manufacturer and
          exporter of automotive filters based in Qinghe County, Xingtai City, Hebei Province, China.
        </p>
        <p>
          We treat your information with care and only collect what is necessary to respond to your inquiry
          and, where applicable, to do business with you. Please read this policy so you understand your
          rights and how to exercise them.
        </p>

        <nav class="toc" aria-label="Policy contents">
          <strong>Contents</strong>
          <ol>
            <li>Who we are</li>
            <li>Information we collect</li>
            <li>How we use your information</li>
            <li>How we share your information</li>
            <li>International data transfers</li>
            <li>Data retention</li>
            <li>Security of your information</li>
            <li>Your rights</li>
            <li>Cookies and similar technologies</li>
            <li>Children&rsquo;s privacy</li>
            <li>Changes to this policy</li>
            <li>How to contact us</li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>{site.companyName}</strong> is a professional automotive filter manufacturing company that
          integrates production, research and development, sales and after-sales service. We specialize in
          automotive air filters, cabin filters, oil filters, fuel filters, wiper blades, transmission filter
          screens and LED lights, serving export buyers on an OEM / ODM / private-label basis.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our registered and operating address is {site.address}. You can reach us at{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or by WhatsApp at {site.whatsapp}.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
        <p>
          We collect information in two ways: information you provide to us directly, and limited technical
          information collected automatically when you browse the website.
        </p>
        <h3>2.1 Information you provide directly</h3>
        <p>When you submit an inquiry form, send us an email, or message us on WhatsApp, we may collect:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your name or the name of your contact person;</li>
          <li>Your company name (if provided);</li>
          <li>Your email address;</li>
          <li>Your telephone, mobile or WhatsApp number (if provided);</li>
          <li>Your country or target market (if provided);</li>
          <li>The content of your message, which may include product models, OE numbers, vehicle types, target markets, order quantities, and any other details you choose to share.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The inquiry form on our website asks only for the fields that are marked. You are not required to
          provide more than what is necessary for us to respond to your request. Our website does not collect
          payment-card details; payments, if any, are arranged separately through channels you agree with us
          in writing.
        </p>
        <h3>2.2 Information collected automatically</h3>
        <p>
          Like most websites, our hosting infrastructure may automatically record limited technical data when
          you access the site. This may include your IP address, browser type and version, device type,
          operating system, referring page, pages visited, and the date and time of each request. This
          information is used to keep the website secure, diagnose technical problems and understand aggregate
          usage. It is not used to build a personal profile of you, and we do not use it to make decisions that
          produce legal or similarly significant effects concerning you through fully automated means.
        </p>

        <h2>3. How we use your information</h2>
        <p>We use the information we collect for the following purposes:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>To respond to inquiries.</strong> To answer your questions, prepare quotations, and follow up on product, sample, pricing, MOQ, lead-time and certification requests.</li>
          <li><strong>To fulfill a business relationship.</strong> To process sample approvals, orders, production, packing, logistics and after-sales service where you choose to do business with us.</li>
          <li><strong>To communicate with you.</strong> To send you information you have requested, and — only where permitted — occasional updates about new products or services relevant to your business.</li>
          <li><strong>To improve the website.</strong> To understand how the site is used and to fix errors.</li>
          <li><strong>To meet legal obligations.</strong> To comply with applicable law, respond to lawful requests, and protect our rights and the security of our systems.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Legal bases for processing</h3>
        <p>
          We process your personal information on one or more of the following legal bases: (a) your consent,
          which you may withdraw at any time; (b) the necessity of processing to take steps at your request before
          entering into, or to perform, a contract with you; (c) compliance with a legal obligation to which we
          are subject; and (d) our legitimate business interests in responding to inquiries, developing our
          business relationships and keeping our systems secure, provided those interests are not overridden by
          your rights and freedoms.
        </p>

        <h2>4. How we share your information</h2>
        <p>We do not sell or rent your personal information to third parties. We only share it in the following limited circumstances:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Service providers.</strong> We may use third parties to host our website, process emails, or support communications. These providers only process your information on our instructions and under obligations of confidentiality and security.</li>
          <li><strong>Fulfilment partners.</strong> Where necessary to complete an order, we may share shipping details with freight forwarders, carriers, customs brokers or our banking and logistics partners to the extent required to perform the transaction.</li>
          <li><strong>Legal and safety.</strong> We may disclose information where we believe in good faith that disclosure is required by law, regulation or legal process, or is necessary to protect the rights, property or safety of our company, our customers or the public.</li>
          <li><strong>Business transfers.</strong> In the event of a merger, acquisition or sale of assets, your information may be transferred as part of that transaction, subject to the same protections described here.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. International data transfers</h2>
        <p>
          {site.brand} is based in China and serves customers worldwide. If you contact us from outside
          China, the information you provide will be transferred to and processed in China. We take reasonable
          steps to ensure that any such transfer is carried out securely and that your information continues to
          receive a level of protection consistent with this policy. By using the website and contacting us,
          you understand and consent to this transfer.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Data retention</h2>
        <p>
          We retain personal information only for as long as is necessary to fulfil the purposes described in
          this policy, unless a longer retention period is required or permitted by law. In practice:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Inquiry correspondence is retained while the inquiry is active and for a reasonable period afterwards to allow follow-up;</li>
          <li>Transaction and order records are retained for as long as required by accounting, tax and commercial law;</li>
          <li>Technical logs are retained for a short period for security and diagnostics, then deleted or aggregated.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>7. Security of your information</h2>
        <p>
          We take reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect your information against
          unauthorised access, alteration, disclosure or destruction. These include access controls that limit
          personal information to employees who need it to perform their role (for example, sales or customer
          service), and the use of reputable, security-patched hosting. We review our security practices
          periodically. However, no method of transmission over
          the internet or method of electronic storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute
          security.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
        <p>Depending on where you are located, you may have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Access</strong> — request a copy of the personal information we hold about you;</li>
          <li><strong>Correct</strong> — ask us to correct inaccurate or incomplete information;</li>
          <li><strong>Delete</strong> — ask us to delete personal information in certain circumstances;</li>
          <li><strong>Object or restrict</strong> — object to, or request restriction of, certain processing;</li>
          <li><strong>Data portability</strong> — request that information be provided in a structured, machine-readable format where this right applies;</li>
          <li><strong>Opt out of marketing</strong> — ask us to stop contacting you for marketing purposes at any time.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these rights, contact us at{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or {site.whatsapp}. We will respond within a
          reasonable time and, where a request is declined under applicable law, explain why.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
        <p>
          This website uses a small number of cookies and similar technologies to function correctly and to
          understand aggregate usage. For a full explanation of the cookies we use and how to manage them,
          please see our <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Children&rsquo;s privacy</h2>
        <p>
          This website is a business-to-business site intended for adults acting in a professional capacity.
          We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided
          us with personal information, contact us and we will delete it.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices, technology,
          legal requirements or the services we offer. When we do, we will revise the &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo;
          date at the top of this page. We encourage you to review this page periodically.
        </p>

        <h2>12. How to contact us</h2>
        <p>If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy or our data practices, please contact us:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></li>
          <li><strong>WhatsApp:</strong> {site.whatsapp}</li>
          <li><strong>Mobile:</strong> {site.mobile}</li>
          <li><strong>Address:</strong> {site.address}</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Related documents: <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a> &middot; <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> &middot; <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
